osition":{"commit_sha":"9708181bdcca712ccf01f404e910a1684c456a8e","position":"1786589760237103001-63bf5cf6-21c5-4dfd-9edc-bc0f5fd0225e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4c0e7454f75ef029cee9574264aab1f37ee6a69ff5aa463b60490b4fe7b6dbc5","event_uuid":"ce6a08d8-bf1b-4342-88b8-2b940c97f2ac","position":{"commit_sha":"746b538665f5b3414c5e9d418ad3274932237839","position":"1786589773506536001-ce6a08d8-bf1b-4342-88b8-2b940c97f2ac"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-222_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a8e73304-f7f3-4412-b4c4-68aff489e438","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Status audit 2026-08-05: this epic is in_progress with no Gerrit change, no commit under its full id, and ZERO comments, last event ~13h ago. Children: one closed (ea28), four open and unclaimed. There is no stated blocker, so it is not possible to distinguish deliberate parking from drift. Whoever picks this up should either claim a child and continue, or record why it is parked. Flagging rather than transitioning, because an unexplained status change would destroy the only signal here.","timestamp":1785962687684482001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Coach-move decision: APPROVED and landed move 16 `out-of-loop proof` for T15. Rationale: existing moves 1 (spike), 4 (riskiest-assumption test), and 7 (thin vertical slice) are adjacent but do not capture T15's specific remedy—prove named runtime-only risks through the fastest local or real-target path before codifying the slow loop, with experiment-scoped cleanup. Story clothed-terrazzo-piglet closed after Gerrit 1692 merged at f20e053aad.","timestamp":1786589760237103001}],"created_at":1784918788257547001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2068b24a-0f16-45d3-83b4-206fdd2026dd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"80be-22ed-9d73-436f"}],"description":"Add plan-review criterion T15 \"overlay-derisk\" so plans prove risky runtime mechanisms via a fast out-of-loop experiment BEFORE committing them into a slow, codified delivery loop (CI/CD, IaC apply, provisioning pipeline). Motivation: on infra epics, basic failures (a service that won't boot, a credential that doesn't authorize, a dependency that won't connect, a readiness check that never passes) are discovered only at the END of a long delivery cycle. No existing criterion rewards front-loading those checks into a cheap local run or a manual probe against the real target. This is a CORE built-in change (not project-specific), stack-agnostic (no hardcoded Terraform/docker), routed by the self-gating Pass-1 finder like the other Txx overlays.\n\n## The finalized T15 rubric (design of record)\n\nOVERLAY — apply only when ALL of the following hold; else PASS not-applicable.\n- S1 Codified loop? the mechanism is delivered/validated by pushing through an automated pipeline or an environment/infrastructure apply, not by running or unit-testing code directly.\n- S2 Slow or costly pass? one pass through that loop is slow (minutes-to-hours) or otherwise costly to run.\n- S3 Runtime-only correctness? the change introduces behavior whose correctness only resolves when it actually runs in a realistic environment (boots, authenticates, connects, is authorized, passes readiness) — unreachable by static/unit checks.\n\nWhen applicable, report a finding for each check not satisfied:\n- (a) RISK NAMED — the plan identifies the specific mechanism(s) confirmable only by completing the full loop.\n- (b) FAST OUT-OF-LOOP PROOF — for each named risk, the plan commits to proving it via the fastest feedback path available for that mechanism, outside the slow loop: running the unit locally/emulated where feasible, OR a manual experiment directly against the real target (an interactive call, a one-off CLI/console action, a probe script, a throwaway resource) where local reproduction isn't possible. The experiment is concrete and returns a verdict in minutes, not a delivery cycle. An unnamed \"we'll verify\" / \"we'll check after deploy\" does not satisfy it.\n- (c) PROVE-THEN-CODIFY — the cheap experiment comes before committing the mechanism into the slow loop, so the loop validates an already-proven mechanism.\n- (d) SCOPED CLEANUP — throwaway experiments are cleaned up afterward, with teardown that removes ONLY the artifacts the experiment itself created (the records a probe inserted, the scratch resource it spun up) and touches nothing pre-existing, shared, or persistent; a cleanup step that could delete, reset, or truncate a resource the experiment did not create (e.g. dropping an existing table or wiping a bucket to \"reset\" it) fails this check.\n\nANTI-FP: a manual experiment against the real target is a fully valid proof — never penalize choosing it over local reproduction; many stacks cannot be reproduced locally. A mechanism already proven elsewhere in the codebase needn't be re-proven.\n\nFacet ~ empirical / approach-soundness; exec AGENT (it ground-checks that the named mechanism and named experiment are real/plausible against the codebase). Posture (advisory vs blocking) and block_threshold are NOT decided here — set by the normal registry/review process.\n\n## Required companion change: T10 boundary partition\nThe de-risk (transient experiment) phase and T10's production-hardening phase must not overlap; there is no runtime cross-criterion suppression by design. Fix by partitioning in T10's own rubric text — add a scope clause: \"This overlay evaluates the DURABLE infrastructure — the IaC/config that persists. Transient, throwaway experiments used to de-risk a mechanism before committing it — their creation, isolation, and teardown — are out of scope here.\" (T10 does NOT name T15 or any other overlay.)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] all child tickets are closed\n- [x] `rebar explain T15` renders the criterion with its descriptive name (not the bare id), and\n      `python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide` regenerates\n      `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` with a T15 section, with the criteria-guide and registry\n      validators passing\n- [x] the writing-a-passing-plan guide instructs authors to de-risk out-of-loop before slow delivery loops,\n      evidenced by the T15 guidance appearing in `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`\n- [x] the coach-move decision (add or reject the proposed out-of-loop-proof move) is recorded on this epic\n      as a comment naming the decision and its rationale","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","ea28-020e-8215-4eb9"],["relates_to","80be-22ed-9d73-436f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"bb3e66d3-8a07-406d-8a5f-d6a4f9003390","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8fc2-0306-a9a0-4864","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Add plan-review criterion T15 (overlay-derisk): prove risky mechanisms out-of-loop before slow delivery loops","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2b70059d-e1e1-4a27-a95a-151dfb83f72f","7c81dcc4-7e81-46cc-9340-07a8ddc69f3e","b8ec4297-d42a-4e21-8605-4bea87d478f2","67051306-642a-4202-b818-29dc04baa276","b26bf603-c069-458b-8499-01048600a9eb","bb3e66d3-8a07-406d-8a5f-d6a4f9003390","1ba02e99-f81e-4117-88ec-0220a96a7523","c8e34ac5-b55e-4235-b508-389a9340ec9e","2068b24a-0f16-45d3-83b4-206fdd2026dd","63bf5cf6-21c5-4dfd-9edc-bc0f5fd0225e","ce6a08d8-bf1b-4342-88b8-2b940c97f2ac"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786589773506536002,"uuid":"36b98d78-ec4f-433c-b8f5-88c3454857e5"}